  "answer_text": "The next NBA game is **Game 3 of the 2026 NBA Finals** between the **New York Knicks** and the **San Antonio Spurs**. \n\nThe game takes place on **Monday, June 8, 2026, at 8:30 PM ET** at **Madison Square Garden** in New York City (where the Knicks are returning with a historic 2-0 series lead). \n\nBecause this is a highly anticipated matchup (with the Knicks in their first Finals in 27 years), standard box office tickets are sold out, and secondary market ticket prices have reached historic highs. \n\nYou can find tickets for Game 3 (and subsequent games in the series) through the following marketplaces:\n\n### 1. Official Ticketing Partner\n*   **Ticketmaster:** As the official ticketing partner of the NBA and Madison Square Garden, Ticketmaster is the most secure place to buy verified resale tickets directly from other fans. \n\n### 2. Major Secondary Resale Markets\nBecause tickets are only available via resale, you can compare prices across several major secondary ticket marketplaces:\n*   **SeatGeek:** Often features interactive seat maps of Madison Square Garden to show you the exact view of the court before you purchase.\n*   **TickPick:** A popular choice for high-value games because they do not charge buyers additional service fees, which can save you hundreds of dollars on tickets of this price caliber. \n*   **Vivid Seats** & **StubHub:** Both offer robust buyer-protection guarantees for last-minute playoff ticket purchases.\n\n### 3. Alternative: Official Watch Parties & Immersive Views\nIf the current resale ticket prices\u2014which are starting at several thousand dollars just to get in the door\u2014are out of your budget, you have other official options to experience the game with a crowd:\n*   **Madison Square Garden Watch Parties:** MSG is hosting officially sanctioned watch parties for local fans during the Finals.\n*   **Cosm (Los Angeles/Dallas):** If you are not in New York, venues like Cosm offer ticketed, immersive, \"shared reality\" dome screenings that put you virtually courtside.",
